    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How to learn and recognize grammatical gender",
     "texto": [
      "In German there are three definite articles: **der** (masculine), **die** (feminine) and **das** (neuter).",
      "Some practical clues to recognize them:",
      "1. **Masculine (der):** male beings (**der Mann, der Vater**), male job titles (**der Lehrer**) and many nouns ending in **-er** (**der Computer**).",
      "2. **Feminine (die):** female beings (**die Frau, die Mutter**), job titles ending in **-in** (**die Ärztin**) and nouns ending in **-ung** (**die Wohnung**) or many ending in **-e** (**die Küche, die Lampe, die Tasche**).",
      "3. **Neuter (das):** many names of rooms and household objects (**das Zimmer, das Bad, das Bett, das Haus, das Buch**) and modern loanwords (**das Handy, das Sofa**).",
      "In dictionaries and in Paglot you will always learn the noun together with its article: **der Tisch**, **die Lampe**, **das Bett**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
